      "en": "Ju asked in the group what clothes to bring. Ju, you need to bring swimwear. Very high heels aren't a good idea, because you walk a lot inside the ship. A small block heel is fine, but make it comfortable. I'm the creator of the app, and I came here today to show you the app that will be used at the event, which you'll need to download to browse the game library and see which game teachers can help you. They don't like people wearing flip-flops in the dinner restaurant. At lunch it's the self-service buffet by the pool, so that's fine. Basically, cruise clothing is beachwear during the day and, at night, what you'd wear to a mall. Exactly. So, Ju, since you asked, those are more or less the tips. Wear comfortable clothes, and if you get cold like me, [laughs] I always bring a sweater, even though I've never used it, but I bring it just in case it gets chilly at night, and it's windy everywhere out there, so bring one in case you need it. But definitely bring something white, plus comfortable clothes to wear around the ship, flat sandals and comfortable shoes, sneakers and so on. Another thing people had asked about: pregnant guests, right?",
